This project began as a fork of Seafile Server
(https://github.com/haiwen/seafile-server), originally developed by
Seafile Ltd., and parts of the Go server descend from it. The AGPL
requires that attribution be preserved, which is why this paragraph and
the additional permission in LICENSE.txt are kept verbatim.

Nothing else of the upstream project survives. The C daemon, the Python
web layer, the sync protocol and the on-disk object format have all been
replaced; Silo is a single Go binary speaking its own HTTP API over its
own store format, and no upstream client can talk to it.

